index d10fcfb6b7c8b5c0e4385ba615a93bf9a8fe5d25..989230b657b7d2c4cf210abebef10ec29fb2effb 100644
--- a/tools/airep_v02/README.md
+++ b/tools/airep_v02/README.md
@@ -19,7 +19,8 @@ python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/v02 -v
 | `verify.py` / `verify_node.mjs` | Beta input/profile adapters and corrected observer prerequisites |
 | `profiles.py` | Exact registry/basis identities, self-contained schema evaluation |
 | `reconcile.py` | Named lifecycle facts and missing/contradictory/unevaluated states |
-| `__main__.py` | Key generation, four emit commands, digest, verify and reconcile CLI |
+| `explain.py` | Derived, non-normative claim matrix retaining native checks and qualifications |
+| `__main__.py` | Key generation, four emit commands, digest, verify, reconcile and explain CLI |
 
 Dependencies are the existing `cryptography`, `jsonschema` and Node/Ajv bundles.
 The producer does not depend on Node. Node is required to run the complete parity
@@ -31,3 +32,21 @@ The cursor is single-writer and in-memory. Persist artifacts and resume with
 `previous=…`/`--previous`. It is not a concurrent writer coordinator, production
 key manager or authenticated remote checkpoint. Caller-supplied evidence must
 describe actual observations; valid signatures do not make reports true.
+
+## Explain existing v0.2 evidence (non-normative)
+
+`python3 -m tools.airep_v02 explain --input examples/v02/fixtures/complete.json`
+renders a claim matrix; add `--json` for the same semantics as JSON. It accepts
+the same artifact-array input and operator options as `reconcile`, including
+`--bindings`, `--revocation`, `--independence-policy` and `--profile-bases`.
+`--out` writes either format to a new file. Exit zero means evaluation completed,
+including negative results. Saved reconciliation output is not an input format.
+
+This is a **derived explanatory view, not a new AIREP conformance layer**.
+Claim names, context fields and `explanatory_status` are NON-NORMATIVE rendering
+labels. Native checks, statuses, counts and all per-record class channels remain
+visible. A null native status plus explanatory `NOT_EVALUATED` marks enforcement
+and relying-party claim predicates that the reconciler does not evaluate; no
+acceptance rule is invented. Signature validity is not event truth; MISSING is
+not non-occurrence. See the [worked example](../../examples/v02/EXPLAIN.md) for
+commands, field meanings and the enforcement/effect boundary.
